1. Release 2 Brief
Assessment 3 continues directly from Assessment 2 – Release 1. Each team will complete the Agentic AI software application by extending the existing Release 1 system with a shared non-containerised Multi-Agent Server, new Release 2 agentic-loop review modes, local pre-commit security testing, post-commit CI/CD endpoint testing, and cloud deployment to either Microsoft Azure or Amazon Web Services (AWS).

The project focuses on:

Completion of the integrated Agentic AI software application from Release 1
Retention of the Release 1 non-containerised local AI-Mode, MCP Server, and RAG Server
Implementation of one shared non-containerised local Multi-Agent Server using Planner, Worker, and Reviewer agents
Human review within the Multi-Agent workflow
Extension of the existing shared non-containerised agentic loop with:
Multi-Agent Workflow Review
Testing Report Review
Cloud Deployment Report Review
Local pre-commit security scans executed when committing code
Post-commit CI/CD testing in which each student tests two endpoint functions of their assigned backend/API service
Local deployment of the integrated application, with AI-Mode, MCP, RAG, and the Multi-Agent Server running as non-containerised local services accessible from the frontend UI through the backend/API
Cloud deployment of the integrated group application to either Microsoft Azure or AWS
Cloud deployment with AI-Mode, MCP, RAG, and the Multi-Agent Server disabled by default
Optional bonus marks for enabling selected AI services in the cloud and implementing cloud security controls
Technical report includes:
each student’s updated architecture and design flow showing the Multi-Agent Server and deployment flow
the group cloud reference architecture
each student’s pre-commit security testing report
each student’s post-commit CI/CD endpoint testing report
each student’s local and cloud deployment report
agentic-loop review outputs for the Multi-Agent workflow, testing reports, and cloud deployment reports
the corresponding agentic-loop review/validation logs
Important Rule: An individual feature will not be marked separately from the integrated group application. A non-integrated individual feature will receive a mark of zero for the relevant working-software criteria.

Cloud Baseline: AI-Mode, MCP, RAG, and the Multi-Agent Server must be disabled by default in the required cloud deployment. Enabling these services in the cloud is optional and assessed only through the Bonus Marks section.

Report Submission File Name: ONE report submission per group (submitted by one person from the group). Duplicate group submission will not be marked. Report file name: group-<your group number>.pdf

